## 2. GGUF Split: Validate Shard Count Against `split.count` Before Opening All Shards

**Component:** `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — `gguf_split_paths()`

**Responsibilities:** Resolves the shard paths of a split model from any shard's filename. Currently checks that each shard file exists but does not verify that the number of files found matches the `split.count` metadata inside shard 1 (which is only read later by `GgufModel::validate_split`). A partially-downloaded model where shard 3 of 4 exists but shard 2 does not produces a confusing "missing shard" error naming shard 2, but a model where all files exist yet one is a zero-byte placeholder passes `gguf_split_paths` and fails later in `GgufFile::open`.

**Proposed change:** After building the path list, verify each file is non-empty (at least the 8-byte GGUF magic + version header). This catches zero-byte placeholders from interrupted downloads without opening the full file.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@ -38,6 +38,12 @@
         std::string p = any;
         p.replace(at - 5, 5, num);
         if (!std::ifstream(p, std::ios::binary))
             throw std::runtime_error("missing model shard " + p + " (shard " + std::to_string(i) + " of " +
                                      std::to_string(n) + "; is the download complete?)");
+        // A zero-byte file passes the existence check but cannot be a GGUF.  Check the header size
+        // without reading the whole file.
+        {
+            std::ifstream probe(p, std::ios::binary | std::ios::ate);
+            if (probe.tellg() < 8)
+                throw std::runtime_error("model shard " + p + " is empty or truncated (shard " +
+                                         std::to_string(i) + " of " + std::to_string(n) + ")");
+        }
         out.push_back(std::move(p));
     }
     return out;
```

**Verification cases:**
1. A directory with `model-00001-of-00002.gguf` (valid) and `model-00002-of-00002.gguf` (zero bytes): `gguf_split_paths` throws naming shard 2 as empty.
2. Two valid shards: the function returns both paths unchanged.

